@c ============================================================
@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

DSMR is a Debian 13 (Trixie) packaging of the classic
qmail/vpopmail/dovecot mail stack.  It assembles seven source packages
into a coherent, reproducible email server installation suitable for
hosting multiple virtual mail domains on a single machine.

@section Design Philosophy

@itemize
@item
@strong{djbware at the core.}  qmail is used as the MTA exactly as D.@:J.@:
Bernstein designed it: a small-process pipeline architecture where each
component runs under its own uid and communicates through the queue.
The sagredo-dev patchset adds TLS, DKIM, SPF, SRS, and recipient
checking without altering qmail's security model.

@item
@strong{Daemontools supervision.}  All qmail services run under
daemontools @command{supervise}, started by @command{svscan}.  Services
restart automatically on failure; logs are captured by @command{multilog}
in tai64n format.

@item
@strong{PostgreSQL for virtual users.}  vpopmail is compiled with
@option{--enable-auth-module=pgsql}.  All virtual domain user data
(passwords, home directories, quotas) lives in a PostgreSQL database.
Clear-text passwords are never stored.

@item
@strong{Dovecot 2.4 via SQL.}  Dovecot 2.4 removed its native vpopmail
and checkpassword passdb drivers.  dovecot-vpopmail bridges this gap by
querying the PostgreSQL vpopmail table directly via dovecot's SQL passdb
driver.

@item
@strong{Debian packaging conventions.}  Binaries land under @file{/usr},
runtime state under @file{/var/lib/qmail}, configuration is accessible
at @file{/etc/qmail} (symlink).  Services, users, and groups are created
by package postinst scripts; no manual setup steps are required for a
fresh installation.
@end itemize

