@section Component Roles

@table @strong
@item qmail-smtpd
Receives inbound SMTP connections on port 25 (open) and port 587
(authenticated).  Applies DNSBL, SPF, and HELO-DNS checks.  Uses the
chkuser patch to verify recipient existence against vpopmail before
accepting the DATA phase.

@item qmail-queue
Atomically enqueues accepted messages to @file{/var/lib/qmail/queue/}.

@item qmail-send
The queue runner.  Reads new messages from the queue and dispatches
them to @command{qmail-local} (local recipients) or @command{qmail-remote}
(external recipients).

@item qmail-local
Delivers to local recipients.  Reads @file{/etc/qmail/virtualdomains} and
@file{/var/lib/qmail/users/assign} to resolve virtual addresses to
Unix users.  Executes @file{.qmail} delivery instructions.

@item vdelivermail
vpopmail's delivery agent.  Called by @file{.qmail-default} in each
virtual domain directory; delivers into the appropriate user's
@file{Maildir/}.

@item qmail-remote
Connects to external SMTP servers.  Applies TLS opportunistically and
signs outbound messages with DKIM via @command{spawn-filter}.

@item vchkpw
vpopmail's authentication binary.  Setuid root, owned @code{root:vchkpw}.
Called by the port-587 @command{qmail-smtpd} process to verify SMTP AUTH
credentials against the PostgreSQL vpopmail table.

@item Dovecot
Provides IMAP (port 143, STARTTLS required) and IMAPS (port 993).
Authenticates virtual users via SQL passdb against the PostgreSQL
vpopmail table; authenticates Unix system users via
@file{/etc/dovecot/system-passwd}.
@end table

